---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { CATEGORIES, GITHUB_URL } from '../data/site';

const hue = Object.fromEntries(CATEGORIES.map((c) => [c.key, c.hue]));
const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — Hozz"
  description="What this website collects (nothing) and what the Hozz app does with your Apple Health data (keeps it on your device until you send it somewhere you own)."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main id="main">
    <section class="section prose-section" style={`--tint: ${hue.respiratory}`}>
      <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>The short version: nothing here is watching you.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          This page covers two separate things — this website, and the Hozz app.
          Neither collects anything about you.
        </p>

        <div class="prose">
          <h2>This website</h2>
          <p>
            The site is static files served by Cloudflare Pages. There is no
            analytics script, no tag manager, no advertising pixel, no A/B testing
            and no cookie of any kind. Nothing on the page tries to work out who
            you are.
          </p>
          <p>
            Typefaces are served from this domain rather than a font CDN, so
            loading the page does not tell a third party that you visited. The
            page loads no third-party resources at all.
          </p>
          <p>
            Cloudflare handles the connection and keeps operational logs, the way
            any web host does. That is outside my control and covered by
            Cloudflare's own privacy policy. I do not receive per-visitor data from
            it and have not enabled any visitor analytics.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you follow a link to GitHub, that is GitHub's site under GitHub's
            policies.
          </p>

          <h2>The Hozz app</h2>
          <p>
            Hozz is early alpha. It works, but its coverage is still partial.
            Its design is already fixed on these points, and they are the reason
            the project exists:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Hozz has no account system, because there is no service to sign in to.</li>
            <li>
              Hozz has no server, database or relay of mine. Your data never passes
              through infrastructure I run.
            </li>
            <li>
              Hozz collects no analytics, telemetry or crash reports. Diagnostics
              stay on the device and redact sample values, credentials and
              destination secrets.
            </li>
            <li>
              Hozz never puts your Health data in iCloud. Health-derived files on
              the device are protected and excluded from device backups.
            </li>
            <li>
              Credentials for a destination you configure live in the Keychain on
              that device and are not synced. They are scoped to one destination
              and are never handed to a redirect that leaves the host you set up.
            </li>
            <li>
              Nothing is sent anywhere until you have configured a destination and
              confirmed it. There is no default destination, because a default
              would be a place I chose.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Once you export data to a destination, that copy is yours to look
            after. If you send it to a server, that server's operator — probably
            you — decides what happens to it next.
          </p>

          <h2>Checking any of this</h2>
          <p>
            Hozz is GPL-3.0 and developed in the open, so none of the above has to
            be taken on trust. The behaviour described here is meant to be proven
            by tests rather than by this page.
            <a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener">Read the source</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            If this policy changes, the updated date below changes with it. Last
            updated {updated}.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose-section h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 1.5rem + 2.2vw, 3.1rem);
    margin-block: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .prose {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .prose ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .prose li::marker {
    color: var(--tint);
  }
</style>
